ason":2024,"team":"LV","distance":0.7202,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"DAL","distance":0.7641,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Mike McCarthy"},{"season":2025,"team":"LV","distance":0.7696,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Chip Kelly"},{"season":2022,"team":"IND","distance":0.7834,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Frank Reich"}],"defense":[{"season":2025,"team":"NO","distance":0.2092,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Brandon Staley"},{"season":2025,"team":"WAS","distance":0.3016,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"BUF","distance":0.3036,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"DAL","distance":0.3133,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"JAX","distance":0.3389,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Anthony Campanile"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Cardinals are 3-5 through week 8 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 238 to 175. The offense ranks 19th in EPA per play and the defense 26th in EPA allowed, so neither side has stood out much yet. What sets them apart is the 2nd fewest backs in the backfield in the league.","offense":"The Cardinals offense has been a little below average by EPA per play so far. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Schematically, they stand out for the 2nd fewest backs in the backfield and the 2nd lowest RPO rate in the league. Jacoby Brissett has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Trey McBride, who has drawn 27% of the targets.","defense":"The Cardinals defense has been well below average by EPA allowed per play so far. It has been much better against the run than the pass, ranking 7th and 31st. Josh Sweat has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is Budda Baker, who has 3.5 sacks, after doing little as a pass rusher a year ago. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is an eight man box rate that ranks 11th lowest in the league.","special":"The Cardinals have been one of the most conservative teams on fourth down, going for it on only 14% of their short-yardage chances. Their kickers have made 90% of field goals, which is well above average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into tight ends, about 10% of the money on the books.","players":"Jacoby Brissett has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,719 yards. Trey McBride has been the clear top target with 27% of the looks and 544 receiving yards. The backfield has been a committee led by Jeremiyah Love and Tyler Allgeier. On defense, Budda Baker leads the team with 3.5 sacks.","coaching":"Mike LaFleur is calling the offense as head coach and Nick Rallis is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2022 Jets under Mike LaFleur and the 2024 Raiders. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Saints under Brandon Staley and the 2025 Commanders.","trends":"The offense went from 23rd in EPA per play in 2025 to 19th so far this season, a modest improvement. The defense moved from 27th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 26th so far this season, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was play-action rate, which went from 25% to 16%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}